     This Protection does not consider `lookback_period` as it only looks at the latest trade.
 
+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` tracks a streak of consecutive losing trades - not total or accumulated profit, but how many losses in a row just happened. It looks at trades closed within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), starting from the most recent trade and counting backwards for as long as trades keep closing with a profit below `required_profit`. As soon as a trade closes with profit at or above `required_profit`, the streak is considered broken.
+
+If the streak reaches `trade_limit` or more, trading will stop for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+By default, a single `MaxConsecutiveLosses` entry protects both scopes at once: it locks the specific pair once *that pair* has `trade_limit` consecutive losses, and it locks trading bot-wide once the bot's overall trade history (across all pairs) has `trade_limit` consecutive losses. Set `only_per_pair` to `true` to disable the bot-wide lock and only guard individual pairs. To use different thresholds or cooldowns for the per-pair and bot-wide behavior, configure two separate `MaxConsecutiveLosses` entries (one with `only_per_pair: true`).
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a streak of losing longs.
+
+`required_profit` determines the profit threshold below which a closed trade counts as a "loss" for the streak. This should normally not be set and defaults to 0.0 - any trade that closed with a negative result counts towards the streak.
+
+The below example stops trading for a pair (and, since `only_per_pair` isn't set, bot-wide) for 12 candles after 3 losing trades occurred back-to-back within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "required_profit": 0.0
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
+!!! Note
+    Once the cooldown period elapses, new trades on the affected pair(s) are automatically allowed again - no manual intervention is required. Like other protections, triggering `MaxConsecutiveLosses` is surfaced through the bot's usual notification channels (e.g. Telegram/webhook) as a protection trigger message.
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
